---
title: "Reference"
---

Reference pages are information-oriented descriptions of the machinery. They should be accurate, structured, and easy to look up.

## Add Reference Here

Use this section for stable facts such as:

- Commands, flags, environment variables, and configuration files.
- Public APIs, schemas, model fields, events, and generated assets.
- Operational limits, supported versions, and compatibility notes.

Reference can include examples, but it should not become a tutorial or how-to guide.
